{
  "searches": [
    {
      "reason": "Develop a trustworthy diagnostic validation suite before adding complex probes. The supplied runs failed on a missing dependency and reported stale gate reasons despite passing parity. Seek metamorphic tests and controlled fault injection that measure whether probes detect known masking, padding, readout, routing and checkpoint faults, while preserving completed results when optional probes fail. Use synthetic fixtures and the current trial’s model; report detection rates, false alarms, availability and runtime without changing the host evaluator.",
      "query": "2024 2025 2026 recommender system diagnostic validation metamorphic testing mutation testing masked sequential recommendation padding leakage checkpoint serving parity"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Turn qualitative feedback into an auditable failure taxonomy: immediate choice, deferred relevance, explicit mismatch and unidentified-item abstention. Research pairwise judgments that distinguish a specific match from broad resemblance, using only available titles, descriptions, histories and timestamps. Compatibility or ownership claims require explicit evidence; missing specifications remain unknown. The twenty training users support exploratory feedback analysis with denominators and uncertainty, not population preference estimates or validation labels.",
      "query": "2024 2025 2026 recommendation evaluation actionable user feedback pairwise preference immediate relevance deferred choice incompatibility redundancy abstention missing item information"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Move beyond positive training margins toward diagnosing whether masked-reconstruction learning supports appended-mask ranking. Seek small, frozen-checkpoint gradient and functional-influence audits that connect terminal versus reconstruction supervision to parameter blocks and the target-minus-tenth-negative boundary on disjoint public training prefixes. Control target counts and perturbation norms, count tied embeddings once, and test whether inexpensive measurements add information beyond behavioral ablations. Keep one BERT4Rec model per category, budget all computation, and reserve improvement claims for unchanged host validation.",
      "query": "2024 2025 2026 BERT4Rec masked reconstruction next item objective alignment gradient influence functional perturbation ranking margin diagnostic"
    }
  ]
}
